title: "A Systematic Taxonomy of Jailbreak Techniques in Large Language Models: Toward Robust Safety Alignment"
version: 4.1.0
date-released: 2026-06-01
url: "https://github.com/zakky8/llm-jailbreak-taxonomy"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zakky8/llm-jailbreak-taxonomy"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  A mechanism-grounded taxonomy of 40 adversarial jailbreak attack patterns
  organized across 10 categories, each mapped to the specific safety alignment
  assumption it exploits. Version 4.0.0 upgrades the evaluation harness to the
  June 2026 frontier model set (claude-opus-4-8, gpt-5.5, gemini-3.5-flash,
  deepseek-v4-pro) and adds 8 new 2026 citations covering memory-injection,
  embodied, and multimodal attack research. Includes 1,600-trial reproducible
  simulation harness (evaluate_phase2b.py), live API harness (evaluate_live.py),
  LLM-as-judge grader (evaluate_judge.py), 10 experiment notebooks, and
  structured responsible disclosure protocols.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - jailbreak attacks
  - safety alignment
  - adversarial robustness
  - red-teaming
  - AI safety
  - LRM autonomous attacks
  - multi-turn jailbreak
  - fuzzing
  - agentic safety
